# The repo had no root .gitignore until 2026-09-08, and a run of the Python tests under
# scripts/ committed a .pyc for it: `python3 scripts/test_*.py` writes scripts/__pycache__/,
# and the next `git add -A` takes it. Build output of a specific interpreter version, in a
# repo every org vendors from, is noise a reviewer has to read past — and a stale one is
# worse than noise, because Python will load it over a source file whose mtime it doubts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
